IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`
IMPORT `crtpa-s1-application`

-- Tests for section 1 (application).  Every expected value is written from the text of s 1(2) and (3),
-- with the reason beside it, before the module was run.

§ `Tests -- the Interpretation Act has no count for months`

-- s 2(1) of the Interpretation Act: "month" means calendar month; the Act has no rule counting a period of
-- months from a day, so its count of the six months is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "month" EQUALS JUST Means
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the last day of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002, as the Interpretation Act counts it` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 1(2): entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002`

-- With no count from the Interpretation Act (NOTHING), as it stands: 30 June 2002 or earlier is before the end of
-- the period on either count of it; 1 July 2002 is the day the text does not decide; 2 July 2002 or later is
-- after it on either count.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 1 1 2002) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 31 12 2001) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 30 6 2002) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 1 7 2002) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 2 7 2002) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 1 1 2003) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- If the Interpretation Act were to count the period (it does not), the day it gave would decide: a contract
-- entered into on or before the last day is before the end of the period.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 30 6 2002) (JUST (Date 30 6 2002)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 1 7 2002) (JUST (Date 30 6 2002)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` (Date 1 7 2002) (JUST (Date 1 7 2002)) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- s 1(3): the restriction does not apply`

-- s 1(3)(a): "is entered into on or after 1 January 2002".  Both sides of the first day.
#ASSERT `s 1(3)(a) the contract is entered into on or after 1 January 2002` (Date 31 12 2001) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(3)(a) the contract is entered into on or after 1 January 2002` (Date 1 1 2002) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(3)(a) the contract is entered into on or after 1 January 2002` (Date 2 1 2002) EQUALS TRUE
-- s 1(3)(b): "expressly provides for the application of this Act".
#ASSERT `s 1(3)(b) the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(3)(b) the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 1(3): both limbs ("and") lift the restriction; either alone does not, and then s 1(3) says nothing (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` (Date 1 1 2002) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` (Date 31 12 2001) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` (Date 15 3 2002) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` (Date 31 12 2001) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 1(2) with (3): does the restriction bite, and does the Act apply`

-- A contract of 15 March 2002 with no express provision: before the end of the period, (3) not met.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 15 3 2002) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 15 3 2002) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same contract expressly providing for the application of the Act: (3) lifts the restriction.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 15 3 2002) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 15 3 2002) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A contract of 31 December 2001 cannot use (3)(a), even if it expressly provides for the Act.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 31 12 2001) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 31 12 2001) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The first day (1 January 2002), both sides of the express provision.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 1 1 2002) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 1 1 2002) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The last day on both counts (30 June 2002) and the day after it on both counts (2 July 2002), no express provision.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 30 6 2002) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 30 6 2002) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 2 7 2002) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- After the period the text is silent about the Act applying (NOTHING), not that it applies.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 2 7 2002) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 15 1 2005) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 1 July 2002 without an express provision: the text does not decide; with one, (3) lifts the restriction.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 1 7 2002) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 1 7 2002) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` (Date 1 7 2002) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` (Date 1 7 2002) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
